<title>HUNGARY: CSOPAK POSTS HIGHER H1 PROFIT, SALES.</title>
<headline>CSOPAK POSTS HIGHER H1 PROFIT, SALES.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six-month period ending June</p>
<p>30.</p>
<p>(Figures in thousands of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>				   Jan-June 1997     Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>    Operating profit	    267,689	vs    226,994</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit		274,738	vs    216,197</p>
<p>    Net sales revenue	 6,252,731	vs  3,471,617</p>
<p>	Net domestic sales    6,243,623	vs  3,463,733</p>
<p>	Net export sales	    9,108	vs	7,884</p>
<p>    Other revenue		  67,346	vs     41,234</p>
<p>    Directs costs of sales  4,274,026	vs  2,065,838</p>
<p>    Indirect costs of sales 5,242,076	vs  2,742,529</p>
<p>    Other expenditures	  170,953	vs    165,522</p>
<p>    Net financial income	 63,066 loss vs     25,534 loss</p>
<p>	Financial revenue	  99,518	vs    101,166</p>
<p>	Financial expenditure   162,584	vs    126,700</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income   70,115	vs     14,737</p>
<p>	Extraordinary revenue   994,657	vs    116,050</p>
<p>	Extraordinary expend.   924,542	vs    101,313</p>
<p>NOTE - Csopak Szovetkezeti Rt is a regional retail holding.</p>
<p>The figures were calculated in accordance with Hungarian</p>
<p>Accounting Standards and are not audited.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4040</p>
</text>
